# UI design

- Compact dashboard. South Florida first. Agent-friendly on iPad.
- Comparison stays above the fold on Compare tabs.
- Verification status must stay visible.
- Home: navigation, alerts, verification. No dense resource lists as the first screen.
- Intelligence Bar is one compact row group — not another set of large cards.
- Prefer professional color, clear hierarchy, and large enough tap targets.
- Codex owns the live agent tool: Home, Compare, Reference, Carrier Resources, formatting, dropdowns, navigation, carrier headers, colors, and hyperlinks.
- Cursor stays out of Home, Compare, Reference, and Carrier Resources unless explicitly assigned one of those areas.
- Only one agent may edit the live workbook at a time. If Codex is working in the sheet, Cursor does not write to it.
- Do not restyle Codex-owned sheets. Backend work stays in `data/`, `scripts/`, `tests/`, and docs.
- Excel export must keep text labels even if logos or images are used.
